I know the mantra is The Dev Team Thinks Of Everything, but there are
limits. From my current game are two examples.

I was dipping arrows in fountains in the first couple of levels, and
released a demon who granted me a wish. Since I was running a Val, I wished
for +3 blessed grey dragon scale mail. As soon as I hit the enter button,
and before my slow machine could process the information, I paniced. I had
written grey with an E. Now I wasn't going to get anything at all, and the
wish was wasted. It's amazing how much panic can occur while waiting for
75MHz to work. Then the message came back

h  gray dragon scale mail

Ha, the Dev Team spells things both ways. I was really worried, but I
shouldn't have been.

Later, around Dlvl 12, when Brun, my Val was about level 10 or so, I ran
into my first succubus. She insulted me, and I killed her. Teach her to
laugh at a Val. A level later, I ran into a second succubi. I wasn't paying
a lot of attenion, but I got the messages about removing my armor, then
removing my helm, and then she ran her hands through my hair!! What? I
looked back at the messages and yep, I was being seduced by a succubi. Wow,
The Dev Team really Does think of Everything. So now I figured I had a Val
of an alternate lifestyle.  

Then I looked at the status line to see how much my stats had improved. I
swear, that was the first time I noticed that Brun was a Man-at-Arms. Nope,
not the helmet, and not the amulet, since both of those were identified. I
couldn't remeber any poly traps, so just for kicks I checked my attributes
(^X) and discovered I had started as a Male Valkry. Bummer, now Brun wasn't
enjoying an alternate lifestyle, he really was male. Maybe that was why the
first succubi laughed at Brun?. Now I could ascend something really
different. I was a bit dissapointed about the lifestyle, but I guess the
Dev team hasn't implemented all of the great ideas.

For the record, I am running 3.4.1 and after the above discoveries, I
checked and found the Male-Val-bug which has since been fixed. It will be a
fun game anyway. 

